#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0328 expect=noViolation domain=PC
#note "Mirrors rulespec CDISC-SEND-0328-nofire-nonpt0h.yaml - the case the old precondition form got wrong. Exactly one PT0H record plus two DUPLICATE PT1H records in the same profile: only PT0H is restricted, so the rule must not fire. The PCELTM=='PT0H' conjunct excludes the PT1H duplicates and PCELTM in the uniqueness key keeps the single PT0H record unique. A regression to the precondition form (flagging any duplicate in a profile containing PT0H) would fire on rows 2-3 and red this scenario."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset PC label="Pharmacokinetic Concentrations"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PCSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PCTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col PCTPTREF type=Char label="Time Point Reference"
col PCSPEC   type=Char label="Specimen Material Type"
col PCELTM   type=Char label="Planned Elapsed Time from Time Point Ref"
---
S1 | PC | 001 | 1 | DRUGX | DOSE1 | PLASMA | PT0H
S1 | PC | 001 | 2 | DRUGX | DOSE1 | PLASMA | PT1H
S1 | PC | 001 | 3 | DRUGX | DOSE1 | PLASMA | PT1H
